 "summary": "Reabsorbs about 5% of filtered NaCl through NCC and stays impermeable to water, so it keeps diluting the fluid. The main site of hormone-regulated Ca²⁺ reabsorption: PTH adds TRPV5 channels. Thiazides block NCC (Na⁺ out, Ca²⁺ in); Gitelman syndrome is a genetic version.",
